# InkOS — Sprint 8 Design Spec: Payroll + 1099-K + Tax Compliance

**From:** Vega (Design Agent)
**To:** Koda (Feature Builder)
**Date:** 2026-04-15
**Stack:** Stack A — Next.js 16.2.3, Tailwind 4, shadcn base-nova, dark-first
**Sprint:** 8 — Payroll + 1099-K + Tax Compliance (Week 19–21)

---

## 0. Pre-Build Rules (carry all 70 from Sprints 1–7 forward, plus these)

71. Migration `20260416000006_payroll_tax.sql` must be confirmed applied before any Sprint 8 UI is written. Tables needed: `payroll_runs`, `payroll_artist_summary`, `tax_forms`, `artist_tax_info`, `payroll_payment_batches`. All 11 RPCs must be present. The deferred FKs (`commission_records.payroll_run_id`, `commission_adjustments.payroll_run_id`) must be live. Dato confirms before Koda writes line 1.

72. **`payroll_artist_summary` is RPC-write-only.** All four DML operations blocked by RLS. Use `mark_artist_payment` for per-artist payment. No `.insert()` or `.update()` on this table — 403 guaranteed.

73. **`approve_payroll_run` and `mark_payroll_paid` and `cancel_payroll_run` are owner-only** — not admin. The UI must gate these actions strictly on `currentMember.role === 'owner'`. Admin users see the buttons greyed-out with a tooltip: "Only studio owners can approve and pay runs."

74. **TIN plaintext NEVER touches the client.** The `decrypt_artist_tin` RPC is called exclusively inside the PDF generation worker job — never in a Server Component, Server Action, or API route that returns data to the browser. The UI shows `tin_last4` only (from `get_artist_tax_info_masked`).

75. **Payroll feature gate:** Check `check_feature_access('payroll')` in every payroll Server Component and Action. On Solo/Studio tier, the entire `/payroll` route tree renders `<UpgradeGate>`. The sidebar "Payroll" nav item is hidden for Solo/Studio via `canDo('payroll.view')`.

76. **`calculate_payroll_run` is idempotent.** After calling it, always refetch run detail — never derive totals client-side. Use `get_payroll_run_detail(run_id)` for the canonical numbers.

77. **`locked_at` on tax forms gates all edit UI.** Before rendering any edit action (void, send, generate PDF), check `form.locked_at`. If set, show `<LockedFormBadge />` only. No edit buttons.

78. **1099-K generation is January-only in the UI.** The "Generate 1099-K for [year]" CTA is rendered conditionally: `new Date().getMonth() === 0` (January). Outside January, show the table of existing forms but replace the CTA with "1099-Ks can only be generated in January." The `generate_1099k` RPC itself has no month restriction — the restriction is UI-only as an operational guardrail.

79. **PDF generation is async via BullMQ worker.** Clicking "Generate PDF" enqueues a job — it does not block the UI. Show a `Generating…` skeleton row while the job runs. Worker writes `pdf_storage_path` back to `tax_forms`. The UI polls (or uses Supabase Realtime) to detect when the path is set, then shows the download link.

80. **`set_artist_tax_info` receives plaintext TIN via Server Action only.** The form POST goes to a Server Action that calls the RPC. TIN input value is never logged, never passed through URL params, never included in error messages. Server Action must `sanitizeTin()` (trim, strip dashes/spaces) before passing to RPC.

---

