## 4. New Payroll Run Wizard — `/payroll/runs/new` (3-step Sheet)

The wizard renders as a `<Sheet side="right" className="w-full max-w-lg">`. Not a separate page — Sheet allows the runs list to remain visible behind it on desktop.

### 4a. Sheet header (persistent across steps)

```tsx
<SheetHeader className="px-6 pt-6 pb-0 border-b border-border pb-4">
  <div className="flex items-center justify-between">
    <SheetTitle className="text-lg font-semibold">New Payroll Run</SheetTitle>
    <SheetDescription className="sr-only">Create a new payroll run for your studio</SheetDescription>
  </div>
  {/* Step indicator */}
  <div className="flex items-center gap-1.5 mt-3">
    {[1,2,3].map(n => (
      <div
        key={n}
        className={cn(
          "h-1 flex-1 rounded-full transition-colors duration-200",
          step >= n ? "bg-primary" : "bg-muted"
        )}
      />
    ))}
  </div>
  <p className="text-xs text-muted-foreground mt-1.5">Step {step} of 3</p>
</SheetHeader>
```

### 4b. Step 1 — Period selection

```
┌─ Step 1: Set Pay Period ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                                                                               │
│  [Use last month ↩]                                                           │
│                                                                               │
│  From                             To                                          │
│  [2026-03-01 ▾]                   [2026-03-31 ▾]                              │
│                                                                               │
│  Label (optional)                                                             │
│  [March 2026 Payroll                          ]                               │
│                                                                               │
│  ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── │
│                                                          [Continue →]         │
└───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

**"Use last month" button:** `variant="outline" size="sm"`. On click: sets `period_start` to first day of last month, `period_end` to last day of last month, pre-fills `label` with `"[Month Name] [YYYY] Payroll"` (e.g., "March 2026 Payroll"). Positioned above the date fields.

**Duplicate period validation:** On Continue, check if a run already exists for the selected period (client-side from the runs list already fetched; server also raises `payroll_runs_studio_period_unique`). If duplicate detected before RPC: show inline error below dates: `<p className="text-xs text-destructive mt-1">A payroll run for this period already exists.</p>`. Button stays disabled.

**Date pickers:** `<Popover> + <Calendar>` (same pattern as Sprint 7 date pickers). `period_end` Calendar is constrained: min = `period_start + 1 day`, max = today.

**Label input:** `placeholder="e.g., March 2026 Payroll"`, `maxLength={80}`. Optional.

**Continue button:** Disabled until both dates are set and `period_start < period_end`.

