### 5d. Timeline

```tsx
<div className="payroll-timeline border-b border-border">
  {PAYROLL_STEPS.map((step, i) => {
    const isCompleted = STEP_ORDER.indexOf(run.status) > i
    const isCurrent = STEP_ORDER.indexOf(run.status) === i
    const ts = STEP_TIMESTAMPS[step]  // draft_at | calculated_at | approved_at | paid_at
    return (
      <div key={step} className="payroll-timeline-step">
        {i < PAYROLL_STEPS.length - 1 && (
          <div className={cn("payroll-timeline-connector", isCompleted ? "payroll-timeline-connector-done" : "payroll-timeline-connector-pending")} />
        )}
        <div className={cn("payroll-timeline-dot", isCompleted ? "payroll-timeline-dot-completed" : isCurrent ? "payroll-timeline-dot-current" : "payroll-timeline-dot-pending")} />
        <span className={cn("payroll-timeline-step-label", isCurrent && "payroll-timeline-step-label-current")}>
          {PAYROLL_STATUS_LABELS[step]}
        </span>
        {ts && (
          <span className="payroll-timeline-step-ts">
            {formatRelativeDate(ts)} · {run[`${step}_by_name`] ?? ''}
          </span>
        )}
      </div>
    )
  })}
</div>
```

`PAYROLL_STEPS = ['draft', 'calculated', 'approved', 'paid']`. Cancelled status: timeline shows all steps greyed with a red X overlay on the current step at time of cancellation. Add `--color-payroll-cancelled` dot + "Cancelled" label.

