## 16. Plain-English Copy — Payroll + Tax Jargon

All inline help text (below form labels, in empty states, in tooltips) uses plain English. Koda copies verbatim — no paraphrasing.

### Payroll action labels

| Action | Button label | Inline help text (shown as `text-xs text-muted-foreground` beneath action or in tooltip) |
|--------|-------------|------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|
| Create run | "New Run" | — |
| Calculate | "Calculate" | "Tally up all approved commissions in this period and preview the payout amounts." |
| Approve | "Approve Run" | "Lock the calculated totals. Commissions can't be added or removed after this point." |
| Mark paid | "Mark Paid" | "Record that you've sent payments to artists. This finalizes the run — no further edits allowed." |
| Cancel | "Cancel Run" | "Remove commissions from this run. They'll return to Approved and can be added to a future run." |
| Recalculate | "Recalculate" | "Re-run the calculation to pick up any commissions approved since last time." |

### Tax jargon explanations

| Term | Tooltip or inline text |
|------|------------------------|
| 1099-K | "US tax form for payments to freelancers who earned $600 or more in a calendar year. Must be filed with the IRS and sent to the artist." |
| TIN | "Taxpayer Identification Number — SSN, EIN, or ITIN depending on the entity type." |
| W-9 | "IRS form collecting an artist's legal name, TIN, and address. Required before you can generate a 1099-K." |
| Backup withholding | "Some payees are required by the IRS to have 24% withheld from payments. Check this only if notified by the IRS." |
| FATCA exempt | "Foreign Account Tax Compliance Act exemption. Applies to certain corporations and entities. Most individual artists leave this unchecked." |
| Exempt payee code | "A 1-digit code on Form W-9 identifying entities exempt from backup withholding. Leave blank if unsure." |
| Locked | "Form is immutable. No further edits, voids, or corrections can be made. Lock after IRS filing." |
| Correction | "A revised 1099-K that supersedes a previously sent form. Issue a correction if any numbers or details were wrong on the original." |

These strings should be placed as `<Tooltip>` content on info icons next to the relevant labels.

