## 19. Skeleton Patterns (6-state standard, Sprint 8 additions)

All data-dependent Sprint 8 components implement 6 states: default, loading, empty, error, hover/active, and (where applicable) locked/read-only.

**Loading skeletons must match the rendered layout.** Koda uses the skeleton shapes specified in each section above. Do not use a single full-page spinner.

**Error state pattern** (consistent with Sprints 1–7):

```tsx
<div className="rounded-lg border border-destructive/20 bg-destructive/5 p-4 flex items-start gap-3">
  <AlertCircle className="h-4 w-4 text-destructive mt-0.5 shrink-0" />
  <div>
    <p className="text-sm font-medium text-foreground">{errorTitle}</p>
    <p className="text-xs text-muted-foreground mt-0.5">{errorMessage}</p>
    {onRetry && (
      <Button variant="ghost" size="sm" className="mt-2 -ml-1 h-7 text-xs" onClick={onRetry}>
        Try again
      </Button>
    )}
  </div>
</div>
```

Specific error messages:
- `payroll_runs_studio_period_unique` RPC error → "A payroll run for this period already exists. View it from the Runs list."
- `locked_at IS NOT NULL` attempt → "This form is locked and cannot be edited."
- TIN missing during 1099-K generation → "Artist has no W-9 on file. Collect tax info before generating the PDF."
- Feature gate error → redirect to `/billing?upgrade=payroll` (not an inline error).

